    "updated_at": "2022-07-07T14:48:24Z",
    "body": "The nodejs symbols uses a nerd-font symbol right now, which will not render correctly if you are not using a nerd font. In the future it will likely switch back to a regular glyph (#3544).\r\nYou can change the symbol with this: \r\n```toml\r\n[nodejs]\r\nsymbol = \"⬢ \"\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs your project-type supported by the [starship package module](https://starship.rs/config/#package-version)? What's the name of the package file?",
